# FDS writes two kinds of output. The small text kind is evidence and belongs in
# the repository: the input files, the run log, the diagnostics and the CSV
# tables every number in the guide was read from. The large binary kind is for
# looking at in Smokeview, is regenerated by re-running the case, and would put
# tens of megabytes of frames into git for no gain.
*.s3d
*.s3d.sz
*.s3dd
*.sf
*.sf.bnd
*.bf
*.q
*.restart
*.smv

# Per-run bookkeeping that says nothing a reader needs.
*_git.txt
*_cpu.csv
*_steps.csv

# Working copies made while translating; en.json and zh.json are the record.
site/chunks/
